     "content": "### The Verdict\n\n**Yes, you should accept this offer.** \n\nSecuring a **$200,000 sign-on bonus** on an L6 offer is an exceptional outcome. You pushed Google to their maximum flexibility, matched your base, and effectively created a **~$758,000 Year 1 compensation package**. \n\nAt this point, you have extracted nearly the maximum financial value possible for an L6 lateral hire. Continuing to negotiate further risks deal fatigue or having the offer pulled.\n\n---\n\n### Compensation Comparison & Multi-Year Trajectory\n\n| Year | Meta (Estimated) | Google (Revised Offer) | Net Advantage at Google |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Year 1** | ~$526,000 | **~$758,000** *($240k base + $48k bonus + $270k RSU + $200k sign-on)* | **+$232,000 (+44%)** |\n| **Year 2** | ~$530,000 | **~$620,000** *($240k base + $48k bonus + $270k RSU + ~$62k Y1 refresh)* | **+$90,000 (+17%)** |\n| **Year 3** | ~$540,000 | **~$683,000** *($240k base + $48k bonus + $270k RSU + ~$125k refreshes)* | **+$143,000 (+26%)** |\n| **Year 4** | ~$550,000 | **~$745,000** *($240k base + $48k bonus + $270k RSU + ~$187k refreshes)* | **+$195,000 (+35%)** |\n| **4-Year Total** | **~$2.15M** | **~$2.80M** | **+$650,000+ total gain** |\n\n*(Note: Assumes target performance ratings and steady stock prices at both companies).*\n\n---\n\n### Why This Is a Strong Win\n\n1. **Immediate De-risking:** The $200,000 cash sign-on completely neutralizes the unvested RSUs you walk away from at Meta. It also shields you against market volatility in Year 1 since it is guaranteed cash rather than equity.\n2. **Substantial 4-Year Upside:** Over a 4-year cycle, you will earn roughly **$650,000+ more** at Google than staying on your current trajectory at Meta (unless Meta rapidly promoted you to IC7).\n3. **Resume / Long-Term Leverage:** Holding senior PM titles at both Meta and Google (L6/IC6) places you in an elite tier for future Director / VP / Head of Product roles across tech.\n\n---\n\n### 3 \"Fine Print\" Details to Confirm Before Signing\n\n1. **Sign-on Clawback Terms:** Confirm whether the $200k is paid in a lump sum in your first paycheck and check the clawback period. (Standard is 100% repayment if you leave within 12 months, or pro-rated over 12\u201324 months).\n2. **Equity Vesting Cadence:** Verify the exact vesting schedule. Google typically uses monthly vesting (or front-loaded schedules depending on the specific grant vehicle).\n3. **Start Date & Bonus Pro-rating:** Clarify how your start date impacts your Year 1 performance bonus (whether it will be pro-rated for the calendar year).\n\n---\n\n### Acceptance Script\n\nYou can reply to the recruiter with enthusiasm to lock it in:\n\n> *\"Thank you for working with the compensation committee to secure this package. Bringing the base to $240,000 alongside the $200,000 sign-on bonus bridges the gap and makes the decision clear.*\n>\n> *I am excited to accept the offer for the Senior Product Manager (L6) role. Please send over the formal paperwork and details regarding start date options and sign-on terms so I can review and sign.\"*",
